# Overlay: turn the local GNSS receiver on. It names the symbol and nothing
# else, so it stacks on either board:
#
#   idf.py -B build-gnss -DSDKCONFIG=build-gnss/sdkconfig \
#          -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.gnsslocal" build
#   idf.py -B build-twatch-gnsslocal \
#          -DSDKCONFIG=build-twatch-gnsslocal/sdkconfig \
#          -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.twatch;sdkconfig.gnsslocal" build
#
# It used to pin the pin and the baud here, and to say the Kconfig symbol
# refused the T-Watch. Both stopped being true in #442: the pin and the baud are
# per-board defaults now -- 44 and 115200 on the Waveshare, 41 and 38400 on the
# T-Watch, each MEASURED and each cited in Kconfig.projbuild -- so an overlay
# that restated one board's pair would hand it to the other board as well. The
# symbol is the whole overlay; the board underneath decides the rest.
#
# Not with sdkconfig.gnssbridge. ATTADIPA_GNSS_LOCAL depends on
# !ATTADIPA_GNSS_BRIDGE, because on the T-Watch both want GPIO 41 and they are
# two stages of one job: the bridge asks the module what it is, this listens to
# the answer.
#
# On the Waveshare this is the product image plus a receiver you soldered on;
# on the T-Watch the module is already fitted, and the pair the bridge measured
# on 2026-09-05 is what the defaults carry.
#
# The pin is settled on both and the level on it is not. H18 in
# docs/research/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md stays PARTIAL because no bench module's TX
# idle voltage has been measured and the S3 is not 5 V tolerant. NOT MEASURED
# is the whole claim -- put a meter on the module's TX before a pad sees it.
CONFIG_ATTADIPA_GNSS_LOCAL=y
